# Day 37

**33km / 10 hours**

This was a longer day than I anticipated. Was a bit of a slower start since it was cold in the morning and the trail began quite sedately on the grassy land. The tall grass I was trudging through featured an excess of snails; they were absolutely everywhere and I had to take care to avoid stepping on them. 

![Can you spot all the snails in this picture?](./snails.avif)

After that there was a section of overgrown plants on the track obstructing the way bit just required some proper waving them aside and descending through a nice forest area to cross a stream which was a breeze. Must require a lot of rain to ever be a concern. 

![A stream to wade through](./stream.avif)

After a while of this I eventually got to the road and then the town where I had planned to have lunch. Except it was raining and I went into a cafe and the prices there were exorbitant. I refused to buy anything on principle. I think it's because it's in a very touristy area so they expect to fleece rich tourists visiting Waitomo to see the glowworms but it definitely solidified my opinion that you should avoid tourist areas if possible. 

Therefore I continued down the road before surely finding some farmland to walk down. The track here was alright but there wasn't much to note, it just dragged on for a while. There was a nice swing bridge but other than that... Just a classic long trek while the rain came and went and came and went over and over. 

![Fun bridge to walk over](./swing-bridge.avif)